From 1d77e0fbf688fff72d254ddf5cbc2724b14e4040 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Barrie <baz.is.me@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 14:14:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] golf: auto-detect current event + fix live in-play
 conditioning
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The golf engine was always emitting the pre-tournament projection because the
live in-play path was silently broken and never wired into the season front
door. This makes `python -m golf.season` ascertain the current PGA event and
its completed rounds on its own and condition predictions accordingly.

Fixes and changes:
- providers/espn.py: define `_to_par` / `_is_out` (were undefined, crashing
  `completed_round_scores` on every refresh — the root cause of the engine
  falling back to pre-tournament). Add event resolver so a name/past event id
  maps to its dated scoreboard (ESPN ignores the `event` query param).
- refresh.py: mount-safe clearing of stale live artefacts.
- season.py: defer to the engine's native auto-route (cmd_simulate /
  cmd_edge condition on live_state.json); mirror the in-play board into the
  canonical predictions.csv; persist the full edge board (outrights + in-play
  matchups/3-balls) to edge_report.csv (was never written, so the card read a
  stale file). Removed the redundant parallel in-play path.
- engine.py: relax the round-group guard to drop only groups naming an
  unmatched player instead of the whole board (was refusing over a single
  bookmaker spelling diff); add a thin-sample staking guard so unmodelled
  players (default-skill fallback) are never staked.
- round_pricer.py: never stake thin-sample players (kept for context, £0 stake).
- simulate_inplay.py: vectorise the ranking loop (~20x faster; full run no
  longer times out).

Tests: 31 golf tests pass, incl. the 17 in-play tests that were red before.
